  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Biography is an exploration of the chemical elements in the human body and the roles they play elsewhere in the world. Each spread is a diagram describing the elements as they exist on the periodic table, the earth's crust, a variety of man-made weapons, medicines and tools, sea water, etc. Each element is identified as a specific colored rectangle and these rectangles continue through the diagrams ... toward the end [they] are interrupted by blind stamped organic shapes and pressure printing."--Big Jump Press website, viewed September 20, 2022.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Printed in Aurora, NY in the spring of 2010 from polymer plates and linoleum on Zerkall Book Vellum. ... Sarah Bryant, Big Jump Press."--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Double-page spreads are numbered 1-9; number 5 appears on sheet that unfolds to double height, number 4 appears on verso of top half of number 5.</subfield>
  </datafield>
